    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_102dc98269d96e4c29ef967f458de89b5375ee3a4325e809fef18c244cb5ecae",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the all-nonzero discrepancy term, additive-twist averages and a Perron integral package the off-diagonal correlation into LHS_ell. Summing sign orientations factorizes its Fourier kernel into chi factors; residue motion cancels the previously removed polar terms, and the zeta functional equation puts the surviving factors into swapped form. This reduces the global comparison to a fixed-prime identity, where coefficient recurrences, boundary decompositions, convolution, and inclusion-exclusion collapse the compatible rational-direction data to the swapped diagonal correlation.",
