    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4a4cfbe72c3dc7cc44ffc64ff0a1e741cb6a67738caf4b53823265b127f1b5c7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Partitioning the shift sets leaves the original divisor correlation unchanged but creates ordered block coordinates in which separate rational directions can be counted. Those strata are needed because an undifferentiated delta-method main term misses contributions, yet ranging over all ordered partitions repeats both a fixed ell-swap and a fixed underlying (m,n) through equivalent shifted systems. The two repetitions have the same multiplicity ell!^2 ell^(2(k-ell)), so division by w_ell removes the redundancy introduced by the refinement without discarding the rational-direction main terms.",
