    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e60aa8fbf32a312e79595f3f4c98ce9069614fca4787b1a6234007e97b68ec66",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The length regime T^ell <= X < T^(ell+1) first caps the recipe at ell swaps; the correlation calculation then partitions into ell rational directions and uses the support of the discrepancies h_j to realize every depth below that cap. All-nonzero discrepancies produce ell-swap terms, while exactly ell' nonzero discrepancies leave the other coordinates on exact rational directions and produce ell'-swap terms, so the discrepancy strata collectively recover the swap orders permitted by X.",
